<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6328" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναγκ-αῖον</span></b> , τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>place of constraint, prison,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				5.4.8
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				14
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>, who adds <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καλλισθένης δὲ ἀνώγεων
				εἶπεν, ὃ δεῖ μᾶλλον λέγεσθαι</span>: but correct
			reading is prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάκαιον</span>
			(preserved in <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				98
			</span></i>, as used by Boeotians), or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀνάκειον,</span> q. v., as in <i><span class="en">
				D.
				45.80
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				98.32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰδοῖον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				1.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1968.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				8(4).133
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>privy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			= sq., <i><span class="en">
				Plaut.
				<u>Rud.</u>
				363
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
